The term engine describes any object which provides [[Wiki/Game Mechanics/Mechanical Power|mechanical power]] when provided with [[Wiki/Game Mechanics/Fuel|fuel]], and something to burn fuel with, like air or oxygen. As well as fluid to cool the engine.

This article looks at the Engine component, a small diesel engine (not to be confused with the [[Wiki/Building/Components/Propulsion|Diesel Engine]] also known as the ''large'' diesel engine).

The small diesel engine provides mechanical power to other components. It accepts a throttle input, allowing the output of the engine to be controlled. It is often the first component placed on any design after basic blocks.


It is commonly paired with a [[Wiki/Guides/Gearbox]] and [[Wiki/Building/Components/Propulsion|clutch]] to provide a full drivetrain. It is possible for the engine to overheat, so it requires a coolant (typically [[Wiki/Game Mechanics/Fluids|water]]) to be pumped in and out of the engine (which is supported by the engine's own suction). The engine requires an in-take of air, and it also requires [[Wiki/Game Mechanics/Fuel|diesel fuel]] to operate. Finally, an [[Wiki/Building/Components/Fluids|exhaust]] is required to pump out the fumes created from the engine's operation.


